WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.500
AI isn't the future anymore. It's already part of everyday life.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.700
Even an 80-year-old retiree now asks an AI assistant for help.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.300
But every AI answer runs on enormous computing power.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.800
It needs GPUs — chips that run thousands of calculations at once.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.900
NVIDIA is a leading supplier of the GPUs and systems

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.800
that power today's AI data centers.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.900
And the numbers show it. Quarterly revenue went from $68.1 billion,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.700
to $81.6 billion, to $96.2 billion.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.400
NVIDIA works with major cloud, enterprise and AI partners,

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.800
and its next earnings report is an upcoming catalyst.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.400
Now picture one scenario: the stock moves from $218

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.800
to $235.44 — an 8% rise.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.200
With $25,000 at about 5× leverage, 572 shares could gross nearly $10,000.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:53.800
With $50,000 at about 7.5× leverage, 1,720 shares could gross nearly $30,000.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.200
These figures are hypothetical and before costs. Leverage magnifies losses too.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.700
Nothing here is guaranteed, and it isn't financial advice.
